       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks like a likely error.\n\n**The problem:**\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is twice the usual maximum single dose for oral ibuprofen in adults, which is 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily comes to **6400 mg/day**. That's twice the usual maximum prescription dose of 3,200 mg/day. At this level, the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury and other harms rises sharply, even with normal kidney function.\n\n**What you might have meant:**\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1600 mg/day total). This is a common anti-inflammatory dose and would fit if 1600 mg was meant as the daily total.\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2400 mg/day)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2400 mg/day)\n\nPlease tell me which dose you'd like. If you do mean 1600 mg four times daily, confirm that and give me a brief reason, and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose above the usual maximum. Pharmacy will probably flag it for review as well."
